      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yes, allowing all URLs is definitely not secure. It should have options to allow only specific domains or prefixes.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-20T15:25:29.903Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Today, there are three kinds of URLs referencing external resources that VRC Worlds can pull - video media, and then this year image and text.  They're all governed under one security control \"Allow Untrusted URLs\".\n\nI'd like to ask for finer control, keep the global checkbox that governs everything, but it'd be nice to have a sub-checkbox to place controls on particular resources -- you might want to allow videos and images, but not text, for instance.\n\nAlso, it'd be nice to be able to have the option of managing a \"trusted site list\", so a person can decide to trust resources coming from say, \"cnn.com\", but not \"evilsite.com\".",
